# /init-project

Initialize the AIDLC harness for a project.

Target: `$ARGUMENTS` (empty folder for a new project, or `--inside-repo` for an existing one)

1. Read `harness/README.md` and `docs/harness/project-initialization.md`.
2. Conduct the configuration interview and fill `project.yaml` values in rounds, one topic at a time: identity, description, owner login, repository, lifecycle profile + areas, stack (dev/test/build commands, deploy CLIs, local URL), skills shared across roles (per-role lists are edited in `project.yaml` afterwards), data sensitivity + protection rule, integrations (design tools, live browser, Open Knowledge, web research), models + readiness.
3. Show the assembled `project.yaml` as a diff and wait for the owner's explicit yes.
4. Run `harness/scripts/init-project.ps1 -Target <path>` with the accepted configuration (never delete anything that exists; report conflicts and stop for explicit choices).
5. Verify: `opencode debug config`, `opencode debug agents`, `harness/scripts/validate-harness.ps1`.
6. Report what was created, what remains for the owner (GitHub scopes/remote/branch protection, credential verification, model readiness), and the first phase entry steps.

The harness never rewrites pre-existing files in a target project without an explicit, recorded owner choice.
